From aead2f0243ae578e3a8265379a9cfd4d86fe4936 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:31:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 109/122] DIMSTYLE: AutoCAD's defaults of the R2007+ variables
 also from DXF

The encoder sets DIMFXL 1, DIMJOGANG 45 degrees, DIMTFILLCLR ByBlock,
DIMMZF and DIMALTMZF 100 when writing R2007+ and R2010+ from older
DWGs, but not from DXF (dat.from_version is the target version then),
where the DXFs before R2007 do not have them, and 0 is not written: so
ACadSharp rejected the DIMSTYLEs of DXFs written as R2010+ and gave
their dimensions the Standard style.

* src/dwg.spec (DIMSTYLE): The defaults also for DWG_OPTS_IN.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/dwg.spec | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/dwg.spec b/src/dwg.spec
index 5edcfbb..178046f 100644
--- a/src/dwg.spec
+++ b/src/dwg.spec
@@ -4459,8 +4459,9 @@ DWG_TABLE (DIMSTYLE)
   SINCE (R_2007a)
     {
       ENCODER {
-        // AutoCAD's defaults. ACadSharp rejects DIMJOGANG 0.
-        if (dat->from_version < R_2007a)
+        // AutoCAD's defaults. ACadSharp rejects DIMJOGANG 0. Also from
+        // DXF, which has them not before R2007, as 0 not at all.
+        if (dat->from_version < R_2007a || (dat->opts & DWG_OPTS_IN))
           {
             if (FIELD_VALUE (DIMFXL) == 0.0)
               FIELD_VALUE (DIMFXL) = 1.0;
@@ -4551,7 +4552,7 @@ DWG_TABLE (DIMSTYLE)
   IF_FREE_OR_SINCE (R_2010b)
     {
       ENCODER {
-        if (dat->from_version < R_2010b)
+        if (dat->from_version < R_2010b || (dat->opts & DWG_OPTS_IN))
           {
             if (FIELD_VALUE (DIMALTMZF) == 0.0)
               FIELD_VALUE (DIMALTMZF) = 100.0;
